{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "page": "10", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/52/52_ppallen_196_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "196", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/1"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_197_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "197", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/2"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_198_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "198", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/3"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_199_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "199", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/4"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_200_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "200", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/5"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_201_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "201", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/6"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_202_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "202", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/7"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_203_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "203", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/8"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_204_thumb.jpg", "page": "9", "label": "204", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/9"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_205_thumb.jpg", "page": "10", "label": "205", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/10"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_206_thumb.jpg", "page": "11", "label": "206", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/11"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_207_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "207", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/12"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_208_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "208", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/13"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_209_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "209", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/14"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_210_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "210", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/15"}, {"image": "/52/52_ppallen_211_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "211", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830/16"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-in-colesville-2-december-1830", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD1", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "205", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26086/26086-0010.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and be numbered with the House of Israel,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16111141989378023607\"><a href=\"#16111141989378023607\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans21\"><span id=\"documenttrans21\">21</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The idea that repentant Gentiles would be adopted into the house of Israel is emphasized in the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>. (See Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=38\" class=\"externalLink\">32</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=91\" class=\"externalLink\">85</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=494\" class=\"externalLink\">488</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=505\" class=\"externalLink\">499</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=519\" class=\"externalLink\">513–514</a> [1 Nephi 14:1–2; 2 Nephi 10:18; 3 Nephi 16:13; 21:6; 30:2].) </p><hr></div></div></aside> for God will not always be mocked, and not pour out his wrath upon those that blaspheme his holy name, for the sword, famines and destruction will soon overtake them in their wild career, for God will avenge, and pour out his phials<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16697226944447760368\"><a href=\"#16697226944447760368\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans22\"><span id=\"documenttrans22\">22</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A contemporary spelling of “vial.” (“Phial” and “Vial,” in <span class=\"title\">American Dictionary.</span>)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">An American Dictionary of the English Language: Intended to Exhibit, I. the Origin, Affinities and Primary Signification of English Words, as far as They Have Been Ascertained. . . .</span> Edited by Noah Webster. New York: S. Converse, 1828.</p></div></div></div></aside> of wrath, and save his elect. And all those who will obey his <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18156720032746672890\"><a href=\"#18156720032746672890\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6221\" topic=\"x6221\" title=\"Commandment\">commandments</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commandment\"><p>Generally, a divine mandate that church members were expected to obey; more specifically, a text dictated by JS in the first-person voice of Deity that served to communicate knowledge and instruction to JS and his followers. Occasionally, other inspired texts...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/commandment\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> are his elect, and he will soon gather them from the four winds of heaven,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16187303959292426588\"><a href=\"#16187303959292426588\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans23\"><span id=\"documenttrans23\">23</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A September 1830 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">revelation</a> defined the elect as those who “hear my voice &amp; harden not their hearts.” The gathering of the elect was also mentioned in an October 1830 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" poptitle=\"Revelation, October\n1830–B [D&amp;C 33]\">revelation</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">Revelation, Sept. 1830–A</a> [D&amp;C 29:7]; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" poptitle=\"Revelation, October\n1830–B [D&amp;C 33]\">Revelation, Oct. 1830–B</a> [D&amp;C 33:6].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> from [p. 205]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and be numbered with the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>House of Israel,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1835930469242472240\"><a href=\"#1835930469242472240\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans21\"><span id=\"documenttrans21\">21</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The idea that repentant Gentiles would be adopted into the house of Israel is emphasized in the <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/book-of-mormon-1830\" poptitle=\"Book of Mormon, 1830\">Book of Mormon</a>. (See Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=38\" class=\"externalLink\">32</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=91\" class=\"externalLink\">85</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=494\" class=\"externalLink\">488</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=505\" class=\"externalLink\">499</a>, <a href=\"/paperSummary/book-of-mormon-1830?p=519\" class=\"externalLink\">513–514</a> [1 Nephi 14:1–2; 2 Nephi 10:18; 3 Nephi 16:13; 21:6; 30:2].) </p><hr></div></div></aside> for God will <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>not always be mocked, and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>not pour out his wrath upon <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>those that blaspheme his holy <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>name, for the sword, famines <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and destruction will soon <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>overtake them in their wild <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>career, for God will avenge, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and pour out his phials<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1362617707486633947\"><a href=\"#1362617707486633947\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans22\"><span id=\"documenttrans22\">22</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A contemporary spelling of “vial.” (“Phial” and “Vial,” in <span class=\"title\">American Dictionary.</span>)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">An American Dictionary of the English Language: Intended to Exhibit, I. the Origin, Affinities and Primary Signification of English Words, as far as They Have Been Ascertained. . . .</span> Edited by Noah Webster. New York: S. Converse, 1828.</p></div></div></div></aside> of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>wrath, and save his elect. <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>And all those who will obey <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>his <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"95614839272537194\"><a href=\"#95614839272537194\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6221\" topic=\"x6221\" title=\"Commandment\">commandments</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Commandment\"><p>Generally, a divine mandate that church members were expected to obey; more specifically, a text dictated by JS in the first-person voice of Deity that served to communicate knowledge and instruction to JS and his followers. Occasionally, other inspired texts...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/commandment\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> are his <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>elect, and he will soon <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>gather them from the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>four winds of heaven,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16852438585960374688\"><a href=\"#16852438585960374688\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans23\"><span id=\"documenttrans23\">23</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A September 1830 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">revelation</a> defined the elect as those who “hear my voice &amp; harden not their hearts.” The gathering of the elect was also mentioned in an October 1830 <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" poptitle=\"Revelation, October\n1830–B [D&amp;C 33]\">revelation</a>. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">Revelation, Sept. 1830–A</a> [D&amp;C 29:7]; <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-october-1830-b-dc-33\" poptitle=\"Revelation, October\n1830–B [D&amp;C 33]\">Revelation, Oct. 1830–B</a> [D&amp;C 33:6].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> from [p. 205]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_205_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_205_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_205.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/52/52_ppallen_205_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/52/52_ppallen_205.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "52", "requestedPageNumber": "10", "numberOfPages": "16", "editorialTitle": "Letter to the Church in Colesville, 2 December 1830", "cle